# Code Citations.md

### Node.js (keycloak-themes/eshop asset builder) ###
# node_modules was never committed here, but nothing was preventing it — a `git add .`
# would have pulled in the entire dependency tree, including platform-specific binaries
# (e.g. @esbuild/win32-x64/esbuild.exe). The theme's compiled output (login.css,
# login.min.css, login.min.js) is intentionally NOT ignored — Keycloak serves those files
# directly from the theme directory, there is no build step at deploy time.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.npm/

